  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 319 AM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nUpper level shortwave energy will lift northeast out of the \nsouthern Plains on Friday and again on Saturday into Sunday \nmorning. Scattered showers and a few storms will be possible at\ntimes with this system. Most of the activity should remain east\nof the area on Friday but could clip the far northwestern \nportions of the area Friday evening into Saturday morning. Much \nof the area may remain dry through Saturday afternoon. Satruday \nevening additional upper level energy will move northeast \nthrough the region. Cloud ice may be limited initially late \nSatruday afternoon and evening, so some periods of drizzle will\nbe possible as lift with the trough moves into the area. As the\nupper level trough moves into the area cloud ice will increase \nand scattered showers and maybe a few thunderstorms will develop\nand move northeast through portions of the area. The better \nchances may be along and southeast of I-44. Overall rainfall \namounts will be on the light side with this system with amounts \ngenerally remaining below one quarter of an inch, and some \nlocations may not see any measurable rainfall with this system. \nNo severe weather will occur with the system this weekend. \n\nThe ensemble model members then show a deep upper level low \nmoving towards and through the region during the early to \nmiddle portions of next week. The 00Z ensemble model members \nstill have difference with the timing and track of the system \nbut those differences are not quite as significant as previous \nruns. There is the potential for widespread showers and \nthunderstorms as the low and associated cold front move through \nthe region, and maybe a severe and flooding risk depending on \nthe exact track and timing of the system. The 00Z model blend \nhas 60-80% chances for showers and thunderstorms from late \nMonday into Tuesday night with linger rain chances on Wednesday.\nThose with interest should continue to monitor the latest \nforecast information.\n\nHighs on Saturday will be around 70 with highs in the lower to\nmiddle 70s on Sunday and Monday. Temperatures then look to cool\nto closer to the normal for the middle to end of next week \nwith highs in the 60s and lows in the 40s.",
